1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,600
Round 7 of the Championship Finals.

2
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:15,600
Get ready, go!

3
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:19,600
Show me rock, John Ken Poe!

4
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:23,600
And the winner is Killua!

5
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:25,600
Yes!

6
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:32,600
Very nice, and now here's your prize, the Sword of Truth.

7
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:36,600
Whoa, hey, check it out, Goan.

8
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:40,600
Card number 83, it goes in a specified slot.

9
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:44,600
Alright, one card down, score!

10
00:00:55,600 --> 00:01:04,600
天使の微笑みで連れ出して

11
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:13,600
孤独でも一人じゃないさ

12
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:19,600
生まれてきたことに必ず意味がある

13
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:23,600
You can fly again!

14
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:25,600
太陽浴びて

15
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:29,600
You can fly away!

16
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:34,600
世界は君の輝きを待ってる

17
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:37,600
大地を踏みしめて

18
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:40,600
君は目覚めてゆく

19
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:46,600
天使の微笑みで連れ出して

20
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:53,600
始まりはいつでも大さくないさ

21
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:59,600
何度でも立ち上がれ

22
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:21,600
大地を守る

23
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:26,600
The problem is, how are we gonna protect the card?

24
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:31,600
Well, we don't have any defensive spell cards, so we should probably get some.

25
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:34,600
Wait! Yeah, you kids!

26
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:37,600
Hand over the Sword of Truth right now!

27
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:41,600
Look, I don't want to have to rough you up, so just do what I tell you!

28
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:44,600
No way, you idiot.

29
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:47,600
Hold on! Fuck!

30
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:51,600
Fuck!

31
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:53,600
You're bluffing, right?

32
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:56,600
I already know that you just started playing the game a little while ago.

33
00:02:56,600 --> 00:03:02,600
You're both newbies, so you haven't obtained any defensive spells yet except for the Sword of Truth.

34
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:05,600
This is Thief!

35
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:10,600
This spell card lets you steal one random card from another player's specified slots.

36
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:14,600
Take this! Thief on! Attack Kilo-

37
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:20,600
Haven't you trained at all, mister? Nice try.

38
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:26,600
I won't give it back the next time.

39
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:32,600
You must be an amateur. This is a game for pro hunters. I'm impressed that you even made it in.

40
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:38,600
But at least we learned something. An attack spell won't kick in until you finish the chant.

41
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:43,600
Yeah, but a strategy like that only works on the very weakest players!

42
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:45,600
Exactly.

43
00:03:53,600 --> 00:04:00,600
If you want a card, you just take it from someone else. Only fools actually participate in tournaments.

44
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:05,600
Understand, boys? If not, you will.

45
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:08,600
They really pissed me off!

46
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:14,600
Just forget it. Those guys are all pros. At least they didn't use brute force.

47
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:19,600
Damn it! Then I've really gotta start focusing hard on building up my spell cards!

48
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:24,600
In that case, I say we should head out to Masadora, the City of Magic.

49
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,600
Sounds like a plan!

50
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:45,600
That's our hideout!

51
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:55,600
We're gonna start off by assigning roles. Everyone here right now will be collecting spell cards for us.

52
00:04:56,600 --> 00:05:03,600
You've probably heard there are 40 different spell cards. We need you to obtain one. Fortress.

53
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:11,600
This is one of the strongest defense spells in existence, and we could certainly use another one of those.

54
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:15,600
It will help us to protect Angel's Breath.

55
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:17,600
What the hell is Angel's Breath?

56
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:24,600
It's a super rare card with an SS rank that no one has ever been able to get their hands on.

57
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:27,600
How can you be sure no one's ever obtained it?

58
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:30,600
There's a spell card called List.

59
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:38,600
Casting it tells you the current conversion number of one card, as well as the number of people who have it.

60
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:41,600
Yeah, okay.

61
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:49,600
The card is incredibly difficult to obtain, because you need to have all 40 spell cards in your possession before you can trade for one.

62
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:56,600
Of course, spell cards are extremely useful in this game, so players tend to use them up.

63
00:05:56,600 --> 00:06:04,600
But now, after a whole lot of searching, we've completed our collection of all 40 spell cards.

64
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:09,600
What we'd like to do is trade them in for an Angel's Breath card right now, but...

65
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:15,600
If you did, you'd have nothing to protect it with. That's why you need a copy of the Fortress, correct?

66
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:25,600
Exactly. That said, in order for this plan to work, what we want you to do is to make a complete list of the 40 spell cards and commit them to memory.

67
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:30,600
Those four Gargayder cards got us 120,000.

68
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:34,600
I know, they were pretty valuable. We don't need to worry about money now.

69
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:38,600
Hey, why don't we buy some food and water? Then we'll head to Masadora.

70
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:41,600
Sure, but first we need a map.

71
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:48,600
The one with information costs 650,000, and the blank one's only 20.

72
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:50,600
Which do you want?

73
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:54,600
The blank one! That way, we get all the fun of filling it in ourselves!

74
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:56,600
You're so positive it's painful.

75
00:06:58,600 --> 00:06:59,600
Game!

76
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:05,600
Wow, this doesn't tell us anything.

77
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:06,600
Let's ask for directions.

78
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:12,600
Head north for 80 kilometers. After you pass by the mountain, you'll get to a lake.

79
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:17,600
You're gonna want to follow that lake north for a little while, and it'll take you right to Masadora.

80
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:21,600
If we hurry, we can do, like, 80 kilometers a day.

81
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:24,600
Assuming that you survive, of course.

82
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:26,600
Huh?

83
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:32,600
That mountain is practically crawling with bandits. Even worse, after you pass the mountain, you'll encounter hordes of monsters.

84
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:34,600
There's bandits? And monsters?

85
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:37,600
Now it's starting to sound like an RPG.

86
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:39,600
Let's see what the monsters look like!

87
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:41,600
Come on, hurry!

88
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:44,600
Alright, move out!

89
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:46,600
Wait, please!

90
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:50,600
I'm begging you.

91
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:51,600
For what?

92
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:53,600
I'd really like to join you if you don't mind.

93
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:55,600
No way. Sorry.

94
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:58,600
But may I ask why not?

95
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:00,600
You'd slow us down.

96
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:04,600
How dare you speak to me that way, you little brat!

97
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:09,600
I could take you out with one hand tied behind my back if I wanted to!

98
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:11,600
That does it.

99
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:18,600
I was only planning to mess with them for a little while, but now I'm going to completely ruin their lives!

100
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:19,600
Hey! Hold it right there!

101
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:28,600
I mean, please! I'll try really hard not to get in your way! I promise!

102
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:34,600
Okay, I have most of the information we need.

103
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:38,600
Then, can you tell us what you've found?

104
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:40,600
Of course. I'll start with number one.

105
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:47,600
I tried a hundred different people in this city, and they all gave the same response when faced with an unusual question.

106
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:51,600
That's typical behavior for non-playable characters.

107
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:53,600
Number two.

108
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:54,600
Book.

109
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:00,600
This copy is real, and this one's a copy Kortipi made.

110
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:02,600
Gain.

111
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:06,600
Kortipi's didn't transform.

112
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:11,600
I believe that might indicate that the game's program didn't recognize Kortipi's card.

113
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:13,600
And three.

114
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:20,600
Shizuku's vacuum seems to function normally in this world, but it won't work on any items that have special abilities of any kind.

115
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:26,600
I think that's because the game was programmed to prevent Nen abilities from being used to collect cards.

116
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:27,600
I see.

117
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:29,600
So?

118
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:33,600
However, these three points indicate yet another possibility.

119
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:40,600
This game isn't taking place in a virtual world. It's based somewhere in the real world.

120
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:42,600
But what do you mean?

121
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:52,600
You see, if any of the players were to actually enter Greed Island, then their souls would fully detach from their bodies and enter the console, leaving their bodies behind.

122
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:55,600
Sending them in physically wouldn't be necessary.

123
00:09:56,600 --> 00:10:03,600
And while separating body and soul might be possible, it would take a lot more than standing in front of a console and using Hatsu.

124
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:08,600
It would make a lot more sense if the players were actually teleported somewhere else entirely.

125
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:13,600
Therefore, the software operating the console has nothing to do with playing the game.

126
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:18,600
Its job is to teleport players who trigger it with Hatsu to this island.

127
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:23,600
That stands to reason, but I don't think I get what it means.

128
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:27,600
The big reward for clearing the game. You remember it?

129
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:29,600
Let's see. What was it?

130
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:38,600
Of all the cards you've found for your specified slots, you can choose three and take them all back to the real world with you.

131
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:44,600
That's right. And that means that every one of these items are available to be used outside of the island.

132
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:52,600
If this game does indeed take place in the real world, then it should be possible to remove all of the treasure without actually having to clear the game.

133
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:54,600
Understood.

134
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:56,600
Book.

135
00:10:57,600 --> 00:11:04,600
So at the moment, we only know a little bit about a few select items. It would be most beneficial to learn about all the cards.

136
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:09,600
To start, we need the spell card called Eye of God.

137
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:13,600
And then we just need to find Finks and Phaeton.

138
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:19,600
Another cheap map, huh?

139
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:23,600
Still, he was carrying a lot of spell cards.

140
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:28,600
Well, wanna split up for now? Let's meet back in Masadoria in a week.

141
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:32,600
We'll see which one of us can kill more players. Make it a race.

142
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:36,600
Okay, but be sure to take their cards first.

143
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:58,600
So what do you think we should do about her?

144
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:05,600
Just ignore her. We'll have a chance to ditch her once the bandits show up.

145
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:08,600
But isn't that kinda mean?

146
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:11,600
What are you talking about? She passed, right?

147
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:16,600
So she's got strong Nen abilities. She can escape if it gets rough.

148
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:26,600
She's keeping up better than I thought she would.

149
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:31,600
Their stamina isn't half bad. Well, for a couple of brats anyway.

150
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:41,600
You ready?

151
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:42,600
Mm-hmm.

152
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,600
Please help us. We beg you.

153
00:12:49,600 --> 00:13:04,600
The disease is spreading.

154
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:11,600
It starts with a mild fever, but then it gets progressively worse and worse until the afflicted finally dies.

155
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:16,600
All we can do is use medicine to keep the fever at bay.

156
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:21,600
Sadly, the medicine only works for about a week.

157
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:27,600
It's also incredibly expensive. And now, we're completely out of money.

158
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:33,600
We're all sick, so we can't even steal what we need like we normally would.

159
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:39,600
Could we catch it? It's probably just part of the gameplay.

160
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:43,600
Help us! My son only has two or three more days to live!

161
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:47,600
Would you be so kind as to give us some money? Every little bit helps.

162
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:50,600
So this is part of the game too, right?

163
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:56,600
Yeah. If we just give them the right amount of money, then they'll probably reward us with some good items or some information.

164
00:13:56,600 --> 00:13:59,600
So, uh, how much do you guys need?

165
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:01,600
80,000 Jenny.

166
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:05,600
But that's all the money we have.

167
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:08,600
Yeah, it sounds like they know everything about us, doesn't it?

168
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:12,600
Excuse me, but I have enough to cover the 80,000 Jenny.

169
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:16,600
Excuse me? We're busy, so shut up for a minute.

170
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:19,600
I'm gonna kill that brat!

171
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:23,600
Okay, we got it. We'll give you the 80,000 Jenny.

172
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:25,600
You really will?

173
00:14:25,600 --> 00:14:28,600
Thank you both so much! You've just saved my poor son's life!

174
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:32,600
I... I'm so cold! So very cold!

175
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:39,600
This is awful! If his body gets even a little bit colder, he's going to die before we can get the medicine into him!

176
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:46,600
If only we had some children's clothes for him! Why don't we have clothes?

177
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:50,600
I guess I could give him what I'm wearing.

178
00:14:51,600 --> 00:15:01,600
Can you really? You're just like angels sent to us from Heaven. Mere words aren't nearly sufficient to express the depth of our gratitude!

179
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:04,600
Oh, no need to thank us.

180
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:06,600
Unless you've got items or info.

181
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:10,600
Hm?

182
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:13,600
We got nothing!

183
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:17,600
We gave all of our clothes away and now we're totally broke, too!

184
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:19,600
Dammit! They're messing with us!

185
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:23,600
I wonder what that was all about.

186
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:28,600
But as soon as we get past this mountain, we'll find lots of monsters, right?

187
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:33,600
Yeah! If we beat a few of them and turn them into cards, we can sell them for cash!

188
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,600
And then we might finally get to start fighting!

189
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:38,600
Time to see what you've got!

190
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:39,600
You've got!

191
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:40,600
You too!

192
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:43,600
I want to see what you've accomplished in your secret training!

193
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:45,600
I can't wait!

194
00:15:51,600 --> 00:15:53,600
This area's really rocky.

195
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:56,600
Let's go for it!

196
00:15:57,600 --> 00:15:58,600
Yeah!

197
00:15:58,600 --> 00:15:59,600
I can't wait!

198
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:03,600
I can't wait!

199
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:05,600
I can't wait!

200
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:07,600
I can't wait!

201
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:09,600
Whoa! There are tons of them!

202
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:11,600
Whoa!

203
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:13,600
Ugh!

204
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,600
Ugh!

205
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:19,600
Gone's attack didn't do anything?

206
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:23,600
I guess punches aren't gonna do it.

207
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:26,600
And there are so many.

208
00:16:26,600 --> 00:16:29,600
To disable one with a single attack?

209
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:39,600
Bingo! We go for the eye!

210
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:41,600
Book!

211
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:43,600
Gone! Just came for the eye!

212
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:45,600
I got it!

213
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:01,600
They're moving around way too much,

214
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:03,600
but otherwise not bad.

215
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:07,600
They were weaker than they looked.

216
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:10,600
Yeah, but after we left it alone for a minute,

217
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:11,600
the card reverted.

218
00:17:11,600 --> 00:17:13,600
We can do this easy, Gone.

219
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:16,600
Every one of these monsters comes with a built-in weakness.

220
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:19,600
Just gotta stay calm and think.

221
00:17:19,600 --> 00:17:20,600
Alright!

222
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:22,600
Now let's head for Masadora!

223
00:17:22,600 --> 00:17:23,600
Yeah!

224
00:17:23,600 --> 00:17:24,600
Yeah!

225
00:17:24,600 --> 00:17:36,020
Oh!

226
00:17:36,020 --> 00:17:43,980
Gold!

227
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:50,180
Uff!

228
00:17:50,180 --> 00:17:52,400
Gold!

229
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:56,400
I'm okay. See? It didn't even hurt.

230
00:17:56,400 --> 00:17:58,400
This one's pretty weak.

231
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:02,400
Yeah, but it's really fast. Let's hurry up and catch it!

232
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:08,400
Damn it!

233
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:14,400
Aim where it's going to be.

234
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:18,400
If you watch closely, you can learn an opponent's pattern of motion.

235
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:22,400
Your eyes are sharp, but you aren't using them properly!

236
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:26,400
It got away from us.

237
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:29,400
You know, if the rest of the monsters are this weak,

238
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:31,400
we're going to get to Masadora in no time.

239
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:33,400
Ugh, don't be so stupid.

240
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:37,400
What if you encounter one that's strong and fast?

241
00:18:45,400 --> 00:18:47,400
Are those bubbles?

242
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:50,400
Huh?

243
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:52,400
It's gone.

244
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:57,400
